-- CASE 3. Josh and Ana build in Palmerston. HYPOTHETICAL: de facto partners; Josh 24, citizen; Ana 17 on the
-- commencement date, a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa. Comprehensive home building contract
-- 1 Dec 2027, $410,000, on land they own; ready 15 Nov 2028. Only Josh will live there.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- s 8(3): Josh is 18 or over, so Ana need not be. s 9(2): one citizen is enough. s 12(4): commencement on or after
-- 28 Apr 2015 and Josh complies, so Ana is exempt from living there.
#ASSERT (`Am I eligible for the first home owner grant` `a comprehensive home building contract` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2027) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2027) 24 FALSE `an Australian citizen` `no grant was paid on an earlier application` FALSE FALSE `never held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia` TRUE FALSE `a de facto partner` FALSE TRUE 17 FALSE `a New Zealand citizen who holds a special category visa` `no grant was paid on an earlier application` FALSE FALSE `never held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `eligible: every applicant meets the eligibility criteria (ss 7(1)(a), 8-12A)`
-- s 13(1)(b): a building contract by owners of land in the Territory.
